<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        DISPOSITION GAP CLOSURE TRANCHE 2, ITEM 1a (agent-output/disposition-gap-closure-t2-design.md
        §3 Item 1a; Gate 1 decision D-1, 2026-08-31). Repoints this formula from
        CASE(TEXT(Argus_Signal__c), ...) onto days-until-peak, so it MIRRORS
        SellMeterService.bandForPeak EXACTLY (<= 30 GREEN, <= 90 YELLOW, else/null RED). This is an
        IN-PLACE formula edit, not a delete+create - <type>Text</type> is unchanged.

        🔴 THE THREE OUTPUT STRINGS ARE A CONTRACT AND ARE BYTE-IDENTICAL TO THE PRIOR FORMULA'S
        VALUES: "Sell now", "Getting Close", "Hold - Not yet". Four reports
        (Dispositions/Readiness_Mix, Readiness_Signal_By_Value_Avk, Portfolio_Sell_Readiness,
        Total_Argus_Value) GROUP on this field's VALUE (verified: all four group, none filters on
        a value), and Disposition_Dashboard_Junior.dashboard-meta.xml groups on the FIELD
        (<groupingColumn>Property_Asset__c.Sell_Readiness_Band__c</groupingColumn>), not a value -
        so preserving the strings is what buys ZERO report/dashboard edits in this tranche. They are
        also byte-identical to lwc/sellMeterList's METER labels and lwc/sellMeterStats's card
        labels. DO NOT CHANGE THEM.

        🔴 THIS FIELD IS NOW NON-DETERMINISTIC - THE MORE IMPORTANT CHANGE THAN THE RE-BUCKETING
        BELOW. It used to be a function of Argus_Signal__c, a manually-maintained picklist that
        only changed when someone edited a record. It is now a function of TODAY() (via
        Peak_Sell_Date__c), so its VALUE can flip from one day to the next with no record edit, no
        metadata diff and no audit trail. An asset silently crosses from "Getting Close" to
        "Sell now" the morning its peak date comes within 30 days.

        Consequence: the four reports named above all GROUP on this field, and
        Sell_Readiness_By_Type (Dispositions folder) sums Readiness_Score__c
        (Readiness_Score__c.field-meta.xml, this folder), which itself now derives from this
        field - so all five reports, plus both Disposition_Dashboard_Junior donuts
        (groupingColumn Property_Asset__c.Sell_Readiness_Band__c, two places), will change from
        one day to the next with nothing to point to. This is CORRECT and INTENDED - it is what
        "days to peak" means - but it is exactly the shape that gets reported as a data bug weeks
        later ("the donut changed and nobody touched anything"). Anyone investigating that report
        should start here.

        Mechanical safety check performed before making this acceptable: a repo-wide grep for
        Sell_Readiness_Band__c and Readiness_Score__c finds no list-view filter, no validation
        rule, no roll-up summary and no SOQL WHERE clause anywhere under force-app. Every consumer
        is a report GROUPING, a dashboard groupingColumn, a permission set field grant, an
        objectTranslation, or a profile field-level-security entry. Nothing branches on the value,
        which is why a value that changes daily is tolerable rather than a functional defect.

        ⚠ THE FORMER 4TH BRANCH IS GONE, DELIBERATELY (design P-4 / Gate 1 D-1). The prior else-
        branch was the literal unresolved-entity string "&#8212;" (not a real em dash) - a
        pre-existing cosmetic defect, not introduced here. Under days-to-peak that branch is
        UNREACHABLE (bandForPeak returns exactly three values and null peak -> RED), so it is
        removed outright: the "&#8212;" donut segment disappears and every asset that sat in it
        moves into "Hold - Not yet". Both are correct under A3 and both are user-visible screen
        changes - see Gate G-1 in the design doc (measure the divergence in usman-dpeg before
        deploy).

        ISBLANK(Peak_Sell_Date__c) is evaluated FIRST, matching bandForPeak's own null check -
        Peak_Sell_Date__c - TODAY() on a null date evaluates to a null comparison (false), which
        would silently fall through to the wrong branch if the null guard were not first.
        <= 30 has NO lower bound, matching bandForPeak: an already-past peak still bands GREEN
        ("sell now") by design.

        ⚠ GATE G-3, UNRESOLVED BY THIS PASS - RECORDED, NOT GUESSED. This field carries no
        <formulaTreatBlanksAs> today (it referenced only a picklist). It now references a Date
        field instead. Whether the Metadata API requires, accepts or rejects that element on a
        Date-referencing Text formula at API 67.0 is NOT exercised anywhere in this repo and
        salesforce-api-context MCP is not configured for this project (.mcp.json carries only the
        `salesforce` server) - so this element is deliberately left ABSENT, unchanged from before
        this edit, rather than guessed. Per the standing rule (ARCHITECTURE.md §3.4's precedent):
        deploy this ONE field as a dry-run first and READ THE FORMULA BACK before any dependent
        change (Readiness_Score__c, item 1b, references this field and must deploy AFTER it).

        A3's stated goal ("Home and the Dashboard can no longer disagree") is only PARTIALLY closed
        by this edit - see the comment in Argus_Signal__c.field-meta.xml in this folder for the two
        disagreements this item does NOT close.
    -->
    <fullName>Sell_Readiness_Band__c</fullName>
    <externalId>false</externalId>
    <formula>IF( ISBLANK(Peak_Sell_Date__c), &quot;Hold - Not yet&quot;, IF( Peak_Sell_Date__c - TODAY() &lt;= 30, &quot;Sell now&quot;, IF( Peak_Sell_Date__c - TODAY() &lt;= 90, &quot;Getting Close&quot;, &quot;Hold - Not yet&quot; )))</formula>
    <label>Sell Readiness Band</label>
    <required>false</required>
    <trackHistory>false</trackHistory>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Text</type>
    <unique>false</unique>
</CustomField>
